# Observable Information Hierarchy

A quantitative market research platform that measures the predictive value of observable information under rigorous validation constraints. The trading system is one consumer of its outputs.

**Mission:** Empirically determine which aspects of financial markets are predictable with the observable information available, how much confidence that prediction deserves, and whether acquiring additional information is justified.

| Level | Status | Latency | Examples |
|-------|--------|---------|----------|
| L0 Raw market data | ✅ in pipeline | Candle close | OHLCV, mark_price, volume |
| L1 Derived features | ✅ in pipeline | Candle close | ATR, trend, liquidity levels, volatility regime |
| L2 Positioning (OI + funding) | ✅ available | Minutes | open interest, funding rate |
| L3 Microstructure / historical order book | ❌ requires ingestion | Milliseconds | order book imbalance, queue dynamics, trade flow |
| L4 Options surface | 🟡 partial | Minutes–hours | implied volatility, skew |
| L5 Macro / cross-asset | 🟡 partial | Hours–days | FRED macro, cross-asset flows |

## Data Availability

| Data | Live | Historical | Free | Phase |
|------|------|------------|------|-------|
| OHLCV | true | true | true | 1 |
| MARK_PRICE | true | true | true | 1 |
| FUNDING | true | true | true | 1 |
| OPEN_INTEREST | true | limited | true | 1 |
| TRADES | true | true | true | 2 |
| ORDER_BOOK | true | false | false | 3 |
| LIQUIDATIONS | limited | false | false | 3 |
| OPTIONS_IV | partial | limited | partial | 3 |
| MACRO_FRED | true | true | true | 2 |

## Integration Roadmap

- **Phase 1:** OHLCV, mark_price, funding, open_interest
- **Phase 2:** trade_flow, multi_exchange_sync, market_breadth, macro_fred
- **Phase 3:** historical_l2, liquidations, options_surface (only if justified)

> OI and funding are L2 — free and practical. Test before expensive L3 microstructure.

